Input: {"question": "What is the birth date of Richard Aldworth?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d00", "start": 0, "end": 144, "text": "Richard Griffin, 2nd Baron Braybrooke Richard Griffin, 2nd Baron Braybrooke (3 July 1750 – 28 February 1825) was an English politician and peer."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d00", "start": 145, "end": 230, "text": "He was known as Richard Aldworth-Neville or Richard Aldworth Griffin-Neville to 1797."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d00", "start": 231, "end": 345, "text": "The only son and heir of Richard Neville Aldworth Neville, he was born on 3 July 1750 in Duke Street, Westminster."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d00", "start": 346, "end": 422, "text": "He matriculated at Merton College, Oxford, on 20 June 1768, was created M.A."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d00", "start": 423, "end": 442, "text": "4 July 1771, D.C.L."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d00", "start": 443, "end": 482, "text": "3 July 1810, and was incorporated LL.D."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d00", "start": 483, "end": 504, "text": "of Cambridge in 1819."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d00", "start": 505, "end": 596, "text": "Neville was Member of Parliament for from 10 October 1774 till the dissolution in 1780, and"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d01", "start": 0, "end": 113, "text": "party are : John Staples, James Byres, Sir William Young, 2nd Baronet, and Thomas Orde-Powlett, 1st Baron Bolton."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d01", "start": 114, "end": 180, "text": "Aldworth was born on 12 December 1750 in Duke Street, Westminster."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d01", "start": 181, "end": 281, "text": "He was the only son and heir of Richard Neville Aldworth Neville and the former Magdalen Calandrini."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d01", "start": 282, "end": 392, "text": "His father was a diplomat who served as MP for Template : Constlk, Template : Constlk, and Template : Constlk."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d01", "start": 393, "end": 470, "text": "His only sibling was sister Frances, who became the wife of Francis Jalabert."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d01", "start": 471, "end": 519, "text": "His maternal grandfather was Francis Calandrini,"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d02", "start": 0, "end": 90, "text": "To the right of the guide, with a spaniel on his knee, is the future 2nd Baron Braybrooke."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d02", "start": 91, "end": 225, "text": "[1] The others of the party are: John Staples, James Byres, Sir William Young, 2nd Baronet, and Thomas Orde-Powlett, 1st Baron Bolton."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d02", "start": 226, "end": 292, "text": "Aldworth was born on 12 December 1750 in Duke Street, Westminster."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d02", "start": 293, "end": 393, "text": "He was the only son and heir of Richard Neville Aldworth Neville and the former Magdalen Calandrini."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d02", "start": 394, "end": 477, "text": "His father was a diplomat who served as MP for Reading, Wallingford, and Tavistock."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d03", "start": 0, "end": 175, "text": "Richard Neville Aldworth Neville Richard Neville Aldworth Neville (3 September 1717 – 17 July 1793), until 1762 Richard Henry Ashcroft, was an English politician and diplomat."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d03", "start": 176, "end": 378, "text": "The only son of Richard Aldworth of Stanlake, by Catherine, daughter of Richard Neville of Billingbear House, he was born on 3 September 1717; through his mother he was descended from Sir Henry Neville."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d03", "start": 379, "end": 520, "text": "He was educated at Eton College, where he was on good terms with Lord Sandwich, Lord Rochford, Lord Orford, Owen Cambridge, and Jacob Bryant."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d03", "start": 521, "end": 579, "text": "On 12 July 1736 he matriculated at Merton College, Oxford."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d03", "start": 580, "end": 614, "text": "Instead of finishing his course at"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d04", "start": 0, "end": 133, "text": "Richard Neville of Billingbear House , he was born on 3 September 1717 ; through his mother he was descended from Sir Henry Neville ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d04", "start": 134, "end": 281, "text": "He was educated at Eton College , where he was on good terms with Lord Sandwich , Lord Rochford , Lord Orford , Owen Cambridge , and Jacob Bryant ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d04", "start": 282, "end": 342, "text": "On 12 July 1736 he matriculated at Merton College , Oxford ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d04", "start": 343, "end": 418, "text": "[ 1 ] Instead of finishing his course at Oxford Aldworth travelled abroad ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d04", "start": 419, "end": 518, "text": "In 1739 he visited Geneva , and he spent every winter there till 1744 , with other English visitors"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d05", "start": 0, "end": 92, "text": "Baron Braybrooke ) GRIFFIN He was born on September 26 , 1783 in Stanlake Park , Berkshire ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d05", "start": 93, "end": 165, "text": "He died on March 13 , 1858 in Audley End , Essex , he was 74 years old ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d05", "start": 166, "end": 223, "text": "Age:74 He is buried in Waltham , St Lawrence Churchyard ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d05", "start": 224, "end": 392, "text": "A child of Richard ( 2nd Baron Braybrooke ) ALDWORTH-NEVILLE ( LATER ) GRIFFIN and Catherine GRENVILLE ( GRIFFIN ) This information was last updated on July 30 , 2015 ."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d05", "start": 393, "end": 513, "text": "Household of Richard Neville ( 3rd Baron Braybrooke ) GRIFFIN He is married to Jane ( Baroness Braybrooke ) CORNWALLIS ("}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d06", "start": 0, "end": 114, "text": "29 Sep 1036 Flandres 2nd-Great-Grandparents Charles Carolingian 17 Sep 879 - 07 Oct 929 [ Courcy g-g-grandmother ?"}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d06", "start": 115, "end": 334, "text": "] Godefrid Halfdansson bef 826 - Jun 885 Gisela Lorraine abt 860 - abt 26 Oct 907 Arnoul Flandre 12 Dec 889 - 27 Mar 965 Adelaide Vermandois abt 917 - 10 Oct 960 Descendants of Richard ( Neville ) de Neville Loading ..."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d06", "start": 335, "end": 358, "text": "Problems or Questions ?"}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0104-ccf8faacde5c:d06", "start": 359, "end": 460, "text": "Privacy Problems If Neville-2060 represents you or a minor child , send a Pr